 To create a multi-column text display in Adobe JavaScript (AJAX) for a textfield, you can use the `textFlow` and `Paragraph` classes. Here's a simple example of how to create a two-column text display:

1. First, make sure you have the TextField and TextFlow classes available in your project. If not, you can include the following code snippet at the beginning of your script:

```javascript
#target flash
import fl.text.TextFormat;
import fl.text.TextFlow;
import fl.text.formatters.WordWrapper;
import fl.text.layout.FlowLayout;
import fl.text.layout.IFlexContainer;
import fl.text.layout.IColumn;
import fl.text.layout.ColumnFormat;
import fl.text.layout.TextLine;
import fl.text.layout.TextBlock;
import fl.text.layout.TextLayout;
import fl.text.layout.TextLineMetrics;
```

2. Next, create a custom TextField that will handle the multi-column layout:

```javascript
class MultiColumnTextField extends TextField {
    private _columns:Array;
    private _textFlow:TextFlow;

    public function MultiColumnTextField(text:String, columns:int = 2, width:Number = 400, height:Number = 200) {
        super(text);
        this._columns = columns;
        this.width = width;
        this.height = height;

        this.createTextFlow();
        this.updateDisplayList();
    }

    private function createTextFlow():void {
        this._textFlow = new TextFlow();
        this._textFlow.wordWrap = true;
        this._textFlow.wordWrapWidth = this.width / this._columns;

        var textFormat:TextFormat = new TextFormat();
        textFormat.font = "Arial";
        textFormat.size = 12;
        this._textFlow.setTextFormat(textFormat);

        this._textFlow.text = this.text;

        this.text = "";
        this.textFlow = this._textFlow;
    }

    override public function updateDisplayList(unscaledWidth:Number, unscaledHeight:Number):void {
        super.updateDisplayList(unscaledWidth, unscaledHeight);

        if (this._textFlow) {
            this._textFlow.wordWrapWidth = this.width / this._columns;
            this._textFlow.update(true);
        }
    }
}
```

3. Now you can use the MultiColumnTextField in your project:

```javascript
var myText:String = "Lorem ipsum dolor sit amet, consectetur adipiscing elit. Integer nec odio. Praesent libero. Sed cursus ante dapibus diam. Sed nisi. Nulla quis sem at nibh elementum imperdiet. Duis sagittis ipsum. Praesent mauris.";

var multiColumnTextField:MultiColumnTextField = new MultiColumnTextField(myText, 2);
addChild(multiColumnTextField);
```

This example creates a two-column text display with the given text. You can adjust the number of columns by passing the desired number to the MultiColumnTextField constructor.

